WEBVTT

cue-001
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:19.500
<v Hannah Clarke>Good morning, everyone. This is the customer onboarding working group. A reminder that Teams is transcribing and our notetaker will draft the minutes; the notice is in the chat. If anyone objects, say so now.</v>

cue-002
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:31.800
<v Hannah Clarke>No objections, thank you. Three items today: the digital account-opening form, the branch pilot plan, and the marketing campaign. Daniel, over to you for the form.</v>

cue-003
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:58.900
<v Daniel Okafor>Thanks, Hannah. The new form is feature-complete. In testing, a new customer finished onboarding in about ten minutes, against twenty-five minutes on the paper process today. The build cost so far is one hundred and twenty thousand dollars, which is inside the approved budget.</v>

cue-004
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:18.300
<v Marco Silva>Two things are still open on our side. The accessibility audit found contrast and screen-reader issues on the identity step, and we need to finish the fallback for when the identity verification provider is down.</v>

cue-005
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:31.700
<v Hannah Clarke>Marco, when can the accessibility fixes be done?</v>

cue-006
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:44.900
<v Marco Silva>I will have the accessibility fixes finished by Friday the sixth of November.</v>

cue-007
00:01:45.600 --> 00:02:07.200
<v Priya Raman>From compliance, the consent and data-use wording on the first screen still needs our review. I will complete the compliance review of the consent wording by Friday the thirtieth of October.</v>

cue-008
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:27.600
<v Hannah Clarke>Good. Item two, the branch pilot. The proposal is to run the form in two branches, Riverside and Old Town, before any wider rollout. Any objections to two branches?</v>

cue-009
00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:38.900
<v Daniel Okafor>None from product. Two branches gives us enough volume without stretching the support team.</v>

cue-010
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:58.100
<v Hannah Clarke>Then that is agreed: the pilot runs in the Riverside and Old Town branches only. On timing, I suggest we launch on Monday the ninth of November.</v>

cue-011
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:16.400
<v Marco Silva>Sorry, Hannah, the ninth falls inside the platform code freeze. The first day we can release is Monday the sixteenth of November.</v>

cue-012
00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:29.800
<v Hannah Clarke>Fair point. Let us correct that: the pilot launches on Monday the sixteenth of November, not the ninth.</v>

cue-013
00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:49.000
<v Daniel Okafor>I will brief the staff in both branches before launch, by Thursday the twelfth of November, and share the support guide with them.</v>

cue-014
00:03:49.700 --> 00:04:10.300
<v Priya Raman>One risk to record. If the identity verification provider is unavailable, customers would be stuck halfway through. Until Marco's fallback is live, branch staff must be able to complete those cases manually.</v>

cue-015
00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:28.600
<v Hannah Clarke>Agreed, let us record that as a risk, with Marco owning the fallback. An open question I would like us to think about: should the mobile app be part of phase one, or only the web form?</v>

cue-016
00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:41.900
<v Daniel Okafor>I would rather not decide that today. We need the pilot numbers first.</v>

cue-017
00:04:42.600 --> 00:05:03.100
<v Hannah Clarke>Then it stays open. Item three, the marketing campaign. Given the new launch date, I propose we defer the campaign to January, once the pilot results are in.</v>

cue-018
00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:12.400
<v Priya Raman>That works for compliance; it gives us time to review the campaign copy.</v>

cue-019
00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:27.700
<v Hannah Clarke>So the marketing campaign is deferred to January. Anything else? No? Thank you all. Next meeting in two weeks.</v>
